Cyclic (runs every N minutes / “cyclic” / “rerun every” style)

Event-based / file watcher / shout / rule triggers

Workflow dependency jobs (has IN/OUT conditions, predecessor/successor links, etc.)

Smart folders / sub-folders (if you only want leaf jobs)

Below is a practical way to do it.

What to treat as “standalone / singleton”

A good “singleton” heuristic (works well in real environments):

Include a job only if:

It has a runnable command/script (command, script, embedded script, or runAs command)

It has a time schedule (days + time window / scheduling object)

It has no dependencies (no INCOND/OUTCOND / “conditions” / “dependsOn” / etc.)

It’s not cyclic

It’s not event-driven (filewatcher, event triggers, rule-based triggers)

Because Control-M JSON formats differ (Export JSON vs Automation API deploy JSON), we’ll implement detection defensively.

This will extract standalone/singleton jobs as you want:

✅ Includes Job:Script with When

✅ Builds script as: FilePath/FileName + Arguments

❌ Excludes workflow deps: eventsToWaitFor

❌ Excludes event/filewatcher: FileName == "fileWatcher.ksh" (or you can add more patterns)

✅ Keeps notification fields (doesn’t disqualify)



